.TH KTX_EXTRACT 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_extract \- extract images from a KTX2 file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
extract [OPTION...] <input\-file> <output>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes selected images of a KTX2 file as PNG, EXR or raw files. Block compressed and Basis
Universal data is decoded or transcoded first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-level, \-\-layer, \-\-face, \-\-depth
Select the image to extract.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Extract every image into the output directory.
.TP
.B \-\-uri <fragment>
Select images with a KTX fragment URI.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Write the raw image data.
.TP
.B \-\-transcode <target>
Transcode Basis Universal data to this target first.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx extract \-\-level 0 tex.ktx2 level0.png
.fi
.PP
.nf
ktx extract \-\-all tex.ktx2 outdir
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx extract \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
